    j = j + "    \"L4: observable=A+B+C site mass is one arbitrary measurement choice; per-component or phase observables give different Φ. The 5-seed mean controls seed sensitivity but not observable choice.\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L5: the broken-closure control still DECAYS heterogeneously (does not instantly flatten to a dead lattice), so its Φ is non-zero — the contrast is closure-vs-failing-closure dynamics, not closure-vs-dead-flat.\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L6: DIFFUSE=0.05 nn coupling is the integration source; with DIFFUSE=0 sites are independent and spatial Φ loses its meaning. Coupling strength is a free toy parameter, not chemistry.\",\n"
    j = j + "    \"L7: same H_012 lineage limits carry — Michaelis-style saturating production chosen for bounded steady state, no compartmentalization/thermodynamics/monomer-pool; abstract model, no chemistry claim.\"\n"
